Let's denote:
- The speed of the first train as \( v_1 = 7 \text{ km/h} \)
- The speed of the second train as \( v_s = x \text{ km/h} \)
- The initial distance between them as \( d = 221 \text{ km} \)

When two objects move towards each other, their relative speed is the sum of their individual speeds. Therefore, the relative speed in this case is:

\[ v_{\text{relative}} = v_i + v_s = 7 \text{ km/h} + x \text{ km/h} \]

The time \( t \) it takes for the trains to meet can be found using the formula:

\[ t = \frac{\text{distance}}{\text{relative speed}} \]

Substituting the known values into get:

\[ t = \frac{221}{7 + x} \]

